  ## Learning Objectives

  By the end of this module, you will be able to:

  - Apply all 8 rules in real-world scenarios
  - Recognize and fix common violations
  - Use the feature checklist effectively

  ## Real-World Scenarios

  ### Scenario 1: Building a New Feature from Scratch

  **Feature:** User profile management system

  **Step 1: Start Undead**
  ```tsx
  // Start with pure zombies
  function UserProfileCard({ user }) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h2>{user.name}</h2>
        <p>{user.email}</p>
        <img src={user.avatar} alt={user.name} />
      </div>
    );
  }

  function UserProfileForm({ user, onSubmit }) {
    return (
      <form onSubmit={onSubmit}>
        <input name="name" defaultValue={user.name} />
        <input name="email" defaultValue={user.email} />
        <button type="submit">Save</button>
      </form>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Step 2: Add Brain Boundary**
  ```tsx
  function UserProfileView({ userId }) {
    const { user, loading, error, updateUser } = useUser(userId);
    
    const handleSubmit = (formData) => {
      updateUser(formData);
    };
    
    if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
    if (error) return <div>Error: {error.message}</div>;
    
    return (
      <div>
        <UserProfileCard user={user} />
        <UserProfileForm user={user} onSubmit={handleSubmit} />
      </div>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Step 3: Check Horde Ratio**
  - Zombies: 2 (UserProfileCard, UserProfileForm)
  - Brains: 1 (useUser hook)
  - Ratio: 2:1 ❌ (Need more zombies or consolidate)

  **Step 4: Verify 3-Click Rule**
  - UserProfileView → useUser (1 click) ✅

  **Step 5: Design for Three Strains**
  ```tsx
  function useUser(userId) {
    const [user, setUser] = useState(null);
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
    const [error, setError] = useState(null);
    
    useEffect(() => {
      fetchUser(userId)
        .then(setUser)
        .catch(setError)
        .finally(() => setLoading(false));
    }, [userId]);
    
    const updateUser = async (data) => {
      try {
        const updated = await updateUserAPI(userId, data);
        setUser(updated);
      } catch (err) {
        setError(err);
      }
    };
    
    return { user, loading, error, updateUser };
  }
  ```

  **Step 6: Avoid Prop Drilling**
  - UserProfileView passes props directly ✅
  - No tunneling through layers ✅

  **Step 7: Co-locate Related Code**
  ```
  features/
    users/
      UserProfileView.tsx
      UserProfileCard.tsx
      UserProfileForm.tsx
      useUser.ts
      userService.ts
  ```

  **Step 8: Name Files Specifically**
  - ✅ `useUser.ts` (not `hooks.ts`)
  - ✅ `userService.ts` (not `utils.ts`)

  **Step 9: Silence the Living**
  - No console.log statements ✅
  - No warnings ✅

  ### Scenario 2: Refactoring Legacy Code

  **Before (Violates Multiple Rules):**
  ```tsx
  // ❌ Started with brains
  function ProductList() {
    const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
    const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all');
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
    
    useEffect(() => {
      console.log('Fetching products...');
      fetch('/api/products')
        .then(res => res.json())
        .then(data => {
          console.log('Products loaded:', data);
          setProducts(data);
          setLoading(false);
        });
    }, []);
    
    const filtered = products.filter(p => {
      if (filter === 'all') return true;
      return p.category === filter;
    });
    
    return (
      <div>
        <select value={filter} onChange={(e) => setFilter(e.target.value)}>
          <option value="all">All</option>
          <option value="electronics">Electronics</option>
        </select>
        {loading ? <div>Loading...</div> : (
          <ul>
            {filtered.map(product => (
              <li key={product.id}>
                <h3>{product.name}</h3>
                <p>{product.price}</p>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </div>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Violations:**
  1. ❌ Started with brains (Rule 1)
  2. ❌ Console statements (Rule 8)
  3. ❌ Mixed concerns (zombie + brain)

  **After (Follows All Rules):**
  ```tsx
  // ✅ Zombie: Pure presentation
  function ProductList({ products, loading, filter, onFilterChange }) {
    if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
    
    const filtered = products.filter(p => {
      if (filter === 'all') return true;
      return p.category === filter;
    });
    
    return (
      <div>
        <select value={filter} onChange={(e) => onFilterChange(e.target.value)}>
          <option value="all">All</option>
          <option value="electronics">Electronics</option>
        </select>
        <ul>
          {filtered.map(product => (
            <ProductCard key={product.id} product={product} />
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    );
  }

  // ✅ Zombie: Product card
  function ProductCard({ product }) {
    return (
      <li>
        <h3>{product.name}</h3>
        <p>{product.price}</p>
      </li>
    );
  }

  // ✅ Brain: Hook
  function useProducts() {
    const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
    
    useEffect(() => {
      fetch('/api/products')
        .then(res => res.json())
        .then(data => {
          setProducts(data);
          setLoading(false);
        });
    }, []);
    
    return { products, loading };
  }

  // ✅ Brain Boundary: Orchestration
  function ProductsView() {
    const { products, loading } = useProducts();
    const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all');
    
    return (
      <ProductList
        products={products}
        loading={loading}
        filter={filter}
        onFilterChange={setFilter}
      />
    );
  }
  ```

  **Improvements:**
  1. ✅ Separated zombies from brains
  2. ✅ Removed console statements
  3. ✅ Better component structure
  4. ✅ Easier to test

  ### Scenario 3: Code Review Checklist

  Use this checklist when reviewing code:

  - [ ] **Start Undead**: Components start as zombies?
  - [ ] **Horde Ratio**: ≥7:1 zombies to brains?
  - [ ] **3-Click Rule**: Can reach brain in ≤3 clicks?
  - [ ] **Three Strains**: Interface handles happy/failure/async?
  - [ ] **No Tunnels**: No prop drilling through 3+ layers?
  - [ ] **Co-location**: Related code kept together?
  - [ ] **Specific Names**: Files have clear, specific names?
  - [ ] **Silence**: No console statements or warnings?

  ## Common Violations Deep Dive

  ### Violation 1: Starting with Brains

  **Problem:**
  ```tsx
  function MyComponent() {
    const [data, setData] = useState();
    const { data: apiData } = useQuery(...);
    // ...
  }
  ```

  **Solution:**
  ```tsx
  // Start with zombie
  function MyComponent({ data, loading }) {
    if (loading) return <div>Loading...</div>;
    return <div>{data}</div>;
  }

  // Add brain boundary
  function MyComponentView() {
    const { data, loading } = useQuery(...);
    return <MyComponent data={data} loading={loading} />;
  }
  ```

  ### Violation 2: Prop Drilling

  **Problem:**
  ```tsx
  <Parent value={value}>
    <Child value={value}>
      <GrandChild value={value}>
        <GreatGrandChild value={value} />
      </GrandChild>
    </Child>
  </Parent>
  ```

  **Solution:**
  ```tsx
  // Move brain to boundary
  function ParentView() {
    const value = useValue(); // Brain at boundary
    return (
      <Parent>
        <Child>
          <GrandChild>
            <GreatGrandChild value={value} /> {/* Direct from boundary */}
          </GrandChild>
        </Child>
      </Parent>
    );
  }
  ```

  ### Violation 3: Generic File Names

  **Problem:**
  ```tsx
  // utils.ts
  export function formatPrice() { ... }
  export function calculateTotal() { ... }
  export function validateEmail() { ... }
  ```

  **Solution:**
  ```tsx
  // formatPrice.ts
  export function formatPrice() { ... }

  // calculateTotal.ts
  export function calculateTotal() { ... }

  // validateEmail.ts
  export function validateEmail() { ... }
  ```

  ### Violation 4: Brains in Zombies

  **Problem:**
  ```tsx
  function CustomerCard() {
    const flags = useFeatureFlags(); // ❌ Brain in zombie
    return <div>{flags.enableNewFeature ? 'New' : 'Old'}</div>;
  }
  ```

  **Solution:**
  ```tsx
  // Brain at boundary
  function CustomerCardView() {
    const flags = useFeatureFlags();
    return <CustomerCard flags={flags} />;
  }

  // Pure zombie
  function CustomerCard({ flags }) {
    return <div>{flags.enableNewFeature ? 'New' : 'Old'}</div>;
  }
  ```

  ## Feature Checklist Walkthrough

  Use this checklist when building new features:

  ### Planning Phase

  - [ ] Identify zombies needed (UI components)
  - [ ] Identify brains needed (logic/hooks)
  - [ ] Plan horde ratio (target ≥7:1)
  - [ ] Design directory structure
  - [ ] Plan navigation paths (target ≤3 clicks)

  ### Implementation Phase

  - [ ] Start with zombies (pure components)
  - [ ] Add brain boundary (orchestration)
  - [ ] Extract hooks/services (logic)
  - [ ] Design interfaces (three strains)
  - [ ] Avoid prop drilling
  - [ ] Co-locate related code
  - [ ] Use specific file names
  - [ ] Remove console statements
  - [ ] Fix all warnings

  ### Review Phase

  - [ ] Verify horde ratio
  - [ ] Test navigation paths
  - [ ] Review for violations
  - [ ] Run checklist

  ## Case Study: Complete Feature Implementation

  **Feature:** Shopping cart with checkout

  **Step 1: Plan Structure**
  ```
  features/
    cart/
      CartView.tsx          # Brain boundary
      CartItem.tsx          # Zombie
      CartSummary.tsx       # Zombie
      useCart.ts            # Brain hook
      cartService.ts        # Brain logic
  ```

  **Step 2: Start with Zombies**
  ```tsx
  function CartItem({ item, onRemove, onUpdateQuantity }) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h3>{item.name}</h3>
        <p>${item.price}</p>
        <input
          type="number"
          value={item.quantity}
          onChange={(e) => onUpdateQuantity(item.id, parseInt(e.target.value))}
        />
        <button onClick={() => onRemove(item.id)}>Remove</button>
      </div>
    );
  }

  function CartSummary({ total, itemCount, onCheckout }) {
    return (
      <div>
        <p>Items: {itemCount}</p>
        <p>Total: ${total}</p>
        <button onClick={onCheckout}>Checkout</button>
      </div>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Step 3: Add Brain**
  ```tsx
  function useCart() {
    const [items, setItems] = useState([]);
    const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false);
    
    const addItem = (product) => {
      setItems([...items, { ...product, quantity: 1 }]);
    };
    
    const removeItem = (id) => {
      setItems(items.filter(item => item.id !== id));
    };
    
    const updateQuantity = (id, quantity) => {
      setItems(items.map(item =>
        item.id === id ? { ...item, quantity } : item
      ));
    };
    
    const checkout = async () => {
      setLoading(true);
      await cartService.checkout(items);
      setItems([]);
      setLoading(false);
    };
    
    const total = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price * item.quantity, 0);
    const itemCount = items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.quantity, 0);
    
    return {
      items,
      total,
      itemCount,
      loading,
      addItem,
      removeItem,
      updateQuantity,
      checkout,
    };
  }
  ```

  **Step 4: Brain Boundary**
  ```tsx
  function CartView() {
    const {
      items,
      total,
      itemCount,
      loading,
      removeItem,
      updateQuantity,
      checkout,
    } = useCart();
    
    if (loading) return <div>Processing...</div>;
    
    return (
      <div>
        <h1>Shopping Cart</h1>
        {items.map(item => (
          <CartItem
            key={item.id}
            item={item}
            onRemove={removeItem}
            onUpdateQuantity={updateQuantity}
          />
        ))}
        <CartSummary
          total={total}
          itemCount={itemCount}
          onCheckout={checkout}
        />
      </div>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Step 5: Verify Rules**
  - ✅ Start Undead: Started with zombies
  - ✅ Horde Ratio: 2 zombies : 1 brain = 2:1 (could add more zombies)
  - ✅ 3-Click Rule: CartView → useCart (1 click) ✅
  - ✅ Three Strains: Handles loading state ✅
  - ✅ No Tunnels: Props passed directly ✅
  - ✅ Co-location: All cart code together ✅
  - ✅ Specific Names: Clear file names ✅
  - ✅ Silence: No console statements ✅

  ## Final Quiz: Identify Violations

  Review this code and identify all violations:

  ```tsx
  // utils.ts
  export function formatPrice(price) {
    console.log('Formatting price:', price);
    return `$${price.toFixed(2)}`;
  }

  export function calculateTotal(items) {
    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
  }

  // ProductList.tsx
  function ProductList() {
    const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
    const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all');
    
    useEffect(() => {
      fetch('/api/products')
        .then(res => res.json())
        .then(setProducts);
    }, []);
    
    const filtered = products.filter(p => {
      if (filter === 'all') return true;
      return p.category === filter;
    });
    
    return (
      <div>
        <select value={filter} onChange={(e) => setFilter(e.target.value)}>
          <option value="all">All</option>
        </select>
        {filtered.map(p => (
          <ProductCard product={p} />
        ))}
      </div>
    );
  }

  function ProductCard({ product }) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h3>{product.name}</h3>
        <p>{formatPrice(product.price)}</p>
      </div>
    );
  }
  ```

  **Violations Found:**
  1. ❌ Generic file name (`utils.ts`)
  2. ❌ Console statement in `formatPrice`
  3. ❌ Started with brains (`ProductList`)
  4. ❌ Mixed concerns (logic + UI in same component)

  **Fixed Version:**
  ```tsx
  // formatPrice.ts
  export function formatPrice(price) {
    return `$${price.toFixed(2)}`;
  }

  // calculateTotal.ts
  export function calculateTotal(items) {
    return items.reduce((sum, item) => sum + item.price, 0);
  }

  // ProductCard.tsx
  function ProductCard({ product }) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h3>{product.name}</h3>
        <p>{formatPrice(product.price)}</p>
      </div>
    );
  }

  // ProductList.tsx
  function ProductList({ products, filter, onFilterChange }) {
    const filtered = products.filter(p => {
      if (filter === 'all') return true;
      return p.category === filter;
    });
    
    return (
      <div>
        <select value={filter} onChange={(e) => onFilterChange(e.target.value)}>
          <option value="all">All</option>
        </select>
        {filtered.map(p => (
          <ProductCard key={p.id} product={p} />
        ))}
      </div>
    );
  }

  // useProducts.ts
  function useProducts() {
    const [products, setProducts] = useState([]);
    
    useEffect(() => {
      fetch('/api/products')
        .then(res => res.json())
        .then(setProducts);
    }, []);
    
    return products;
  }

  // ProductsView.tsx
  function ProductsView() {
    const products = useProducts();
    const [filter, setFilter] = useState('all');
    
    return (
      <ProductList
        products={products}
        filter={filter}
        onFilterChange={setFilter}
      />
    );
  }
  ```

  ## Creative Application Task

  Build a complete feature following all rules:

  **Feature:** Task management system

  **Requirements:**
  - Display list of tasks
  - Add new tasks
  - Mark tasks as complete
  - Filter tasks (all/active/completed)
  - Delete tasks

  **Your task:**
  1. Plan the structure
  2. Start with zombies
  3. Add brain boundary
  4. Verify all 8 rules
  5. Use the checklist

  **Success Criteria:**
  - All 8 rules followed
  - Horde ratio ≥7:1
  - Navigation ≤3 clicks
  - No violations

  ## Key Takeaways

  - **Apply all rules** when building features
  - **Start undead**, add brains when needed
  - **Maintain horde ratio** for better organization
  - **Keep navigation short** (≤3 clicks)
  - **Design for three strains** (happy/failure/async)
  - **Avoid prop drilling**
  - **Co-locate related code**
  - **Use specific names**
  - **Keep code silent** (no console/warnings)

